## Mapping to our code

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src-tauri/src/commands/scaffold.rs` | Add the `push:false` config patch; baseline migration (needs compose up during scaffold) |
| `templates/*/init.mdc` | New data-driven `migrate: { create, apply, types }` section (mirrors `run`); `run.start` += `&& payload migrate`; `run.restart` += re-migrate after `down -v` |
| **new** `src-tauri/src/commands/migrate.rs` | `migrate_checkpoint(project_id)` → the full cycle; returns `{ created?, destructive?, castFailures? }`; exposed to the UI |
| **new** migration rewriter (Rust or small node script) | Takes Drizzle's raw migration + the field-identity map → emits data-preserving SQL (Tier 1–3). The heart of "resolve as best as possible" |
| `src-tauri/src/commands/db_snapshot.rs` (or extend `git.rs`) | `snapshot_db(sha)` / `restore_db(sha)`; wired into `git_commit` (snapshot after) and `git_restore_to_commit` (restore) |
| `src-tauri/src/commands/ai.rs` / chat | After an edit that touches schema files, call `migrate_checkpoint` |

